CLINICAL REASONING SUMMARY
The patient experienced a sudden, severe episode of pelvic cramping coupled with intense, escalating health anxiety due to being severely overdue for cervical screening. Telephone triage identified the necessity to urgently rule out an acute ectopic pregnancy, acute pelvic infection, or a bleeding pelvic mass. Face-to-face assessment was strictly required to perform a physical and speculum examination, ruling out immediate life-threatening pathology. Because the patient's severe agoraphobia acts as a barrier to daytime access, performing the swab immediately established clinical baseline stability, provided immense psychological relief, and definitively negated the need for an emergency hospital transfer.

